# ================================================================================================
# RESULT
# ================================================================================================
#
# Three palettes, all re-run on today's code so plain and split differ in exactly one thing, k<=4:
#
#     tri45sq          9 /  68 /  412 /  1896  =  2,385     (no split possible, no split needed)
#     tri45two         6 /  50 /  263 /  1154  =  1,473
#     tri45two-split   7 /  92 /  705 /  4243  =  5,047      3.4x
#     tri45all        16 / 161 / 1132 /  6295  =  7,604
#     tri45all-split  17 / 227 / 2057 / 14664  = 16,965      2.2x
#
# CONTAINMENT, by exact congruence and not by the builder's window fingerprint: every plain tiling has
# a congruent copy in its split run, AT THE SAME k. 0 lost of 1,473 on tri45two, 0 of 7,604 on
# tri45all. The oracle self-checks first (rotate, reflect and shift each sampled entry off its own
# lattice; it must come back congruent to itself), so a predicate that always said "different" could
# not have produced this.
#
# THE SHELF: 5,313 -> 16,964 tilings, k = 16 / 227 / 2057 / 14664. All 5,313 previously shipped
# tilings are still on it, at the same k, checked the same way on the SHIPPED bytes.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TWO BUGS THIS TURNED UP, both older than the split work and both in what shipped
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# 1. THE SHELF'S DEDUP WAS MERGING DISTINCT TILINGS. build-tri45-shelf.mjs deduped by a WINDOW
#    FINGERPRINT: clip the tiling to a radius-3.2 patch, re-anchor on each face near the origin, take
#    the lexicographically smallest string over the 16 maps k*45deg x mirror. Two DIFFERENT tilings
#    that agree on a radius-3.2 patch collapse into one, and at k=4 with 16 tiles per cell a 3.2 patch
#    is nowhere near enough to tell them apart. Caught because the rebuild left 453 of the 5,313
#    previously shipped tilings with no congruent copy on the new shelf while the per-palette
#    containment against the same sources was exact -- the gap was entirely the fingerprint, merging
#    differently before and after. Replaced with the exact oracle build-euhalf-shelf.mjs already uses:
#    unimodular lattice map, then face-by-face shape match, bucketed by a congruence-invariant
#    signature. Same input, 13,458 distinct by fingerprint against 16,964 by exact congruence -- the
#    old dedup was losing 3,506 tilings, about a fifth of the shelf.
#
# 2. EVERY SQUARE ON THE SHELF WAS FILED AS A TRIANGLE. The reference records hardcoded `n: 3` on
#    every cell polygon, and `n` is what drives the polygon-species facet. tri45sq and tri45all both
#    carry the unit square and the sqrt2 square. Now `n: f.length`.
#
# Also retired here: the 2026-08-13 tables. They predate the gen_alphabet fixes, their own rebuild
# script says 79 of tri45all's 267 vertex types had a sigma-mixed dart orbit and were unusable, and
# two plain runs of tri45all disagree (27 vs 16 at k=1). Everything above is on today's code.
#
# WHAT THIS SHELF STILL CANNOT SAY. k stops at 4 because that is where the runs stopped, not because
# the family does. No slice is topped up from a shallower-but-deeper-reaching source (AL, 2026-08-18).
